{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-ba428ee9-d5eb-4371-848b-9425c276154e","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-9fc12f56e48a5da6","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8010-tmm99ph7/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8010-E002.md","content":"# Document and publish the structured reconciliation log field convention\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic authors and publishes the contribution guideline that specifies the\nstructured reconciliation log field convention (`name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind`)\nfor new controller development in rhods-operator, documents the DSCI key-name\nmigration for operators, and publishes the convention for voluntary adoption by\nexternal operator teams (Cluster Observability Operator: Loki Operator, Tempo\nOperator) per platform policy overlay 0008.\n\n## Scope\n\nContent outline:\n\n- **Contribution guideline** for new controller development specifying:\n  - Required structured fields: `name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind`\n  - camelCase naming rationale (alignment with controller-runtime's structured log key conventions)\n  - The three-problem diagnosis: message-embedded resource identity, non-standard DSCI key names (`Request.Name`/`DSCInitialization`), and missing `resourceKind`\n  - Before/after code examples for converting message-embedded identity to structured key-value pairs\n  - Treatment of cluster-scoped resources (`name` and `resourceKind`, no spurious `namespace`)\n- **DSCI key migration guide**: before/after query examples (e.g., Loki/CloudWatch) for operators who filter on the old `Request.Name`/`DSCInitialization` field names, ensuring the transition (completed in a single release) is documented.\n- **Release notes** documenting the DSCI key-name migration and the log message-string changes.\n- **External publication**: publish the convention for external operator adoption and file tracking issues in the