n  epic work.\n- Strategy risks carried forward: inconsistent adoption and log-consumer regression →\n  E001 Risks/Notes; DSCI query breakage → E001 Risks + E002 migration guide; cloudmanager\n  sequencing → Health Warning with re-split trigger; external adoption delay → E002 Notes.\n- Open questions: all four dispositioned in the summary table, none silently dropped; the\n  field-extension question is explicitly carried into E002's scope with owner named.\n- Staff Engineer corrections (5 tiers, 15 action files, resolved action-file-count\n  question, camelCase, cloudmanager shared reconciler) are applied in E001's scope and the\n  summary's override table.\n- External operators (COO) correctly have no epic — they perform no work; publication is\n  modeled as E002 deliverables, matching the RFE approval comment and overlay 0008.\n- Out-of-scope items (log overhaul, inference gateway logging, dashboards, non-error\n  paths) correctly excluded from both epics.\n\nDocs-authoring check: the strategy's Prerequisites list \"Documentation Support: Pending\nhuman review\" (not Yes), but the P1 documentation HLR independently mandates it, and E002\n(a `docs-authoring` epic blocked by E001 per Rule 11) satisfies the requirement either\nway. No conditional branches exist or are needed.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":35694,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-af6848a0cefe5aaa","agent_id":"a825e9fcfe71f443e","session_id":"2909a9de-3cce-4cc2-ac2e-bb90c9612f5b","uuid":"d99da8f1-6ed5-4b8e-a1d5-c6368c09a1df","timestamp":"2026-10-25T17:32:03.323Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8010 decomposition"}
