{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9a002c2fa0b2095e","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8010-E002\n3\ttitle: Document and publish the structured reconciliation log field convention\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8010\n5\tcomponent: AI Core Platform\n6\tteam: ODH Operator team\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\timplementation_type: docs-authoring\n10\tdependencies:\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-8010-E001\n12\tai_signals:\n13\t  change_specificity: 1\n14\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n15\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n16\t  existing_foundation: 0\n17\t  open_questions: 0\n18\t  external_dependency: 0\n19\t  human_process_gates: -1\n20\t  repo_access: 1\n21\t  architecture_claims: 1\n22\tinvestigation_signals: null\n23\tai_implementability: Medium\n24\tai_implementability_score: 2\n25\tjira_key: null\n26\tbranch: null\n27\tgated_by: null\n28\tgate_failure_impact: null\n29\t---\n30\t# Document and publish the structured reconciliation log field convention\n31\t\n32\t## Description\n33\t\n34\tThis epic authors and publishes the contribution guideline that specifies the\n35\tstructured reconciliation log field convention (`name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind`)\n36\tfor new controller development in rhods-operator, documents the DSCI key-name\n37\tmigration for operators, and publishes the convention for voluntary adoption by\n38\texternal operator teams (Cluster Observability Operator: Loki Operator, Tempo\n39\tOperator) per platform policy overlay 0008.\n40\t\n41\t## Scope\n42\t\n43\tContent outline:\n44\t\n45\t- **Contribution guideline** for new controller development specifying:\n46\t  - Required structured fields: `name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind`\n47\t  - camelCase naming rationale (alignment with controller-runtime's structured log key conventions)\n48\t  - The three-problem diagnosis: message-embedded resource identity, non-standard DSCI key names (`Request.Name`/`DSCInitialization`), and missing `resourceKind`\n49\t  - Before/after code examples for converting message-embedded identity to structured key-value pairs\n50\t  - Treatment of cluster-scoped resources (`name` and `resourceKind`, no spurious `namespace`)\n51\t- **DSCI key migration guide**: before/after query examples (e.g., Loki/CloudWatch) for operators who filter on the old `Request.Name`/`DSCInitialization` field names, ensuring the transition (completed in a single release) is documented.\n52\t- **Release notes** documenting the DSCI key-name migration and the log message-string changes.\n53\t- **External publication**: publish the convention for external operator adoption and file tracking issues in the COO projects (Loki Operator, Tempo Operator). Adoption is voluntary and best-effort per platform policy (overlay 0008 — RHOAI does not install, manage, or control external operator dependencies).\n54\t\n55\tOpen question carried into this epic: whether the convention should specify fields\n56\tbeyond `name`/`namespace`/`resourceKind` (e.g., reconciliation attempt count, error\n57\tcategory) — owner: PM / Observability team. The guideline ships with the three\n58\trequired fields; any extension is pending that decision.\n59\t\n60\t## Acceptance Criteria\n61\t\n62\t- The contribution guideline is published and specifies the required fields (`name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind`), the camelCase naming rationale, and the three-problem diagnosis, with before/after code examples for converting message-embedded identity to structured key-value pairs.\n63\t- The DSCI key migration guide with before/after query examples is included, and the release notes document the DSCI key-name migration and message-string changes.\n64\t- Tracking issues for convention adoption are filed in the external operator projects (Loki Operator, Tempo Operator).\n65\t- The guideline is technically reviewed against the implemented behavior — the documented field names, call-site patterns, and examples match the code as actually shipped in rhods-operator.\n66\t- The guideline's field specification is limited to the required fields (`name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind`); any extension beyond them is explicitly marked as pending the PM / Observability team decision.\n67\t\n68\t## HLR Traceability\n69\t\n70\t- [P1] Document the convention as a contribution guideline for new controller development and publish for external operator adoption — covered.\n71\t\n72\t## Notes\n73\t\n74\t- External operator adoption (COO team) is at their discretion per platform policy overlay 0008; this epic's deliverable is the publication and the tracking issues, not adoption itself.\n75\t- The RFE approval comment explicitly confirms the publish-for-voluntary-adoption approach for external operators.\n76\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bd180cce1c2c6989","agent_id":"af3aa444b2ea17eed","session_id":"2909a9de-3cce-4cc2-ac2e-bb90c9612f5b","uuid":"ad2802e1-17c7-4e56-8190-9b3e1387f6bc","timestamp":"2026-10-25T17:34:09.436Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9a002c2fa0b2095e","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8010 decomposition"}
